      "id": "rider-flank-lab",
      "title": "Rider & Flank Lab",
      "focus": "Rider Attacks, exposed Frontline, and whether +1 Strength and forced placement reward worthwhile positioning.",
      "setup": "Deliberately form a flank in Battle II/III, test Rider Attack from Middle versus Rear, and compare Long March's +1 Strength payoff to repeated Maneuvers.",
      "observations": [
        "Every Force can Maneuver for 1 Action and 1 Command without being Named; Exhausted still cannot initiate",
        "Grey Riders may Maneuver while Exhausted and make an unused Rider Attack after a Maneuver",
        "Dust Riders' first Bonded Maneuver each Battle saves 1 Command",
        "The Long March uses one secret opening Maneuver for two distinct Riders; one Stratagem per player is the maximum",
        "The Flank Was Refused now counters outer-Front flanking without granting a Move"
